    page itself does not make clear.
  </p>

  <h2 id="checklist">The decision checklist before you pay</h2>

  <p>
    Run through this list on any specific course before entering payment details. If you cannot
    honestly check a box, that is information, not a technicality to skip past.
  </p>

  <ol class="scorecard-list">
    <li class="scorecard-item">
      <span class="scorecard-item__circle">1</span>
      <div class="scorecard-item__body">
        <div class="scorecard-item__title">The syllabus has a visible, recent update date</div>
        <p>
          And the module list names current tools, frameworks, or workflows you can cross-check
          against live job postings for your target role.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="scorecard-item">
      <span class="scorecard-item__circle">2</span>
      <div class="scorecard-item__body">
        <div class="scorecard-item__title">The instructor is a named, searchable, current professional</div>
        <p>
          With a verifiable work history you found independently of the course provider's own
          marketing, not just a bio the provider wrote about them.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="scorecard-item">
      <span class="scorecard-item__circle">3</span>
      <div class="scorecard-item__body">
        <div class="scorecard-item__title">Any placement or outcome number came with a sample size and year</div>
        <p>
          And a clear split between full-time offers and internships, plus median rather than only
          average or highest compensation.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="scorecard-item">
      <span class="scorecard-item__circle">4</span>
      <div class="scorecard-item__body">
        <div class="scorecard-item__title">You checked at least one independent review, not just on-page testimonials</div>
        <p>
          On a third-party forum, review site, or professional community, mentioning specific
          modules or instructors rather than vague praise.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="scorecard-item">
      <span class="scorecard-item__circle">5</span>
      <div class="scorecard-item__body">
        <div class="scorecard-item__title">You compared the total cost, including your time, against a cheaper alternative</div>
        <p>
          And can name specifically what the paid option buys you that the free or cheaper path
          cannot.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="scorecard-item">
      <span class="scorecard-item__circle">6</span>
      <div class="scorecard-item__body">
        <div class="scorecard-item__title">The refund policy is clear, findable, and reasonable</div>
        <p>
          Not buried in a support ticket flow, and not conditional on requirements the marketing
          page never mentioned upfront.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="scorecard-item">
      <span class="scorecard-item__circle">7</span>
      <div class="scorecard-item__body">
        <div class="scorecard-item__title">You have a plan to build one real, visible project alongside the course</div>
